# The Vercel deploy carries the public demo surface only (VDE-62): api/index.py
# plus the stdlib-only modules it imports. Everything else here is the platform
# — Postgres, dbt, Dagster, the MCP server — and has no business in a function
# bundle that is deliberately dependency-free (ADR-015).
#
# Written as a denylist. The first draft was an allowlist (`*` then `!api/**`),
# which excluded api/index.py itself and failed the build with "the pattern
# api/index.py defined in functions doesn't match any Serverless Functions".

.venv
_uv
node_modules
dist
var
docs
tests
evals
dbt
sql
transform
mcp
agent-api
demo
landing
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.github
.cursor
.claude

# The demo surface installs nothing (ADR-015). Vercel's Python builder reads
# whichever dependency file it finds, so leaving these up meant it resolved the
# whole platform lockfile — dagster, dbt, psycopg — and reported "Bundle size
# (278.47 MB) exceeds the standard size; optimizing dependencies" for a server
# that imports only the standard library. requirements.txt (empty) is what the
# demo declares instead. .python-version stays: it pins 3.12, and demo_data.py
# needs datetime.UTC, which is 3.11+.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# src/ is the platform too; only src/agent (the demo's import graph) goes up.
src/extractors
src/models
src/orchestration
src/stores
src/transforms
src/validation
src/cli.py
src/prove_kill_mid_stream.py
src/prove_structlog.py
